  "explanation": {
    "id": "bf1339b9-58cf-4972-ab9f-05962e99dbe4",
    "body": "To find the surface area of the part of the plane $2x + 5y + z = 10$ in the first octant, we can use the formula for the surface area of a function $z = f(x, y)$ over a region $D$:$$A = \\iint_D \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial x}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial y}\\right)^2 + 1} \\, dA$$",
    "questionId": "a521d48c-46f0-437c-8156-14e08ac7c154",
